Have got rid of the stale paths/device references by deleting the
whole device then rescanning for it and moving the device special
files back to that device name.

(take note of the SCSI DEVICEID and DEVICE FILE name with more than
one NUM PATH):->
# hwmgr -show scsi -type tape

(delete the device from the hardware manager and its associated device
files):->
# hwmgr -del scsi -did 48

(rescan scsi bus's for any 'new'devices):->
# hwmgr -scan scsi

(a new DEVICE FILE will have appeared in the list of scsi tape
devices)
# hwmgr -show scsi -type tape

(move the DEVICE FILE name to the previously deleted one)
# dsfmgr -m tape33 tape1

Performed the above for each stale path device.

This has done the job of removing the stale PATHS. Pity you have to
delete the whole device to get rid, then re-add it.

Thanks for the help
Marty

