Gareth Owen wrote:
> Can someone tell me how (as superuser) I can raise the maximum per-process
> stack size limit on OSF1 V5.1?
> 
> Individual users can us 
>   ulimit -s <val>
> up to 16384, but my Fortran code would like it to go a little higher.
> 
> Thanks

You need to adjust the following parameters in the proc subsystem:
per_proc_stack_size
max_per_proc_stack_size

As you might guess one sets the default size and one sets what you can 
ulimit -s the value up to. There are similar parameters for the datasize 
as well (ulimit -d).

If you like guis then dxkerneltuner is the tool for you. Otherwise look 
at the manpages for sysconfig. The values get added to the file 
/etc/sysconfigtab and are read at boot time.

