I had similar problem, with the cards not forcing to 100BaseTX Full
Duplex. Cured it with the following checks and mods.

Modify or check your /etc/inet.local file; we have the following line
added

/usr/sbin/lan_config -i ee0 -a 0 -s 100 -x 1

check the man pages on lan_config this has a lot of info about speed
settings

shutdown the box to chevrons and check the speed of your cards : for
example

>>> show eia0_mode
eia0_mode               FastFD (Full Duplex)

it may say Twisted Pair; change it 
>>> set eia0_mode FastFD

Lastly make sure the port on the switch the server is connected is
fixed to Full Duplex-100

You should thereafter get 100BaseTX. Check your /var/adm/messages file
to verify this. Although it may still initially report half duplex,
but the inet.local entry will change it to the intended setting
thereafter.

Martin



