Tom wrote:
> 
> I am new to Tru64 V4.0 and have a quick question. Is there any
> parameter that can be set in printcap or other configuration file that
> allows you to increase the maximum job limit for print queues. The
> default seems to be 1000.
> 
> Thanks

the printcap entry is :mx#nnn: where nnn is the number of BUFSIZ per
printjob. In Tru64 V5.1, this is 8192 bytes (see /usr/include/stdio.h),
which by default limits a printjob to 8 Megabytes. I don't know a
paramieter which limits the number of jobs in a queue...

