> PCI drawer with two QBB. Is it a good solution to spread efficiently I/O 
> between each QBB ? (The database is set to work with 3 RADs. Three db 
> writer process are set in the init.ora file.)
No real answer here. It depends.

If your app is I/O bounded, and you share the bandwidth needed on
different HBAs, it will definetely help. If you are not IO bounded,
the answer is no.

However, it will never hurt.

use 
# collect -sd -i 2
to know the actual BW to disk units.
use 
# dd if=/dev/rdisk/dskXXc of=/dev/null bs=1024k
to know the max BW you can hope in read, and
# dd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/rdisk/dskXXg bs=1024k
to know the max BW you can hope while writing. THIS WILL ERASE THE
PARTITION.

You can make parallel tests if disks are sharing one PCI or one HBA.

As a thumb rule, if you are peaking at 50% of the max bandwidth, you
are likely not to be I/O bounded.

Cheers


