>
> When I try do download any (large enough) file from that host(via ftp
> samba or NFS) I see very large(several seconds) delays on other tcp
> connections. File transfer rate is less then 4
> Mbytes/second(netstat's info), so there should not be a lack of
> bandwith. Looks like some bottleneck in the network subsystem. I've
> checked a responce of programs, running from console - it looks OK.
>
> I've tried to adjust some parameters of 'inet' and 'net' system, that
> could be related to network problems (netisrfair, netisrthreads,
> tcbhashnum, tcbhashsize, some others). Nothing changed.
>
> Almost no paging. CPU 90% idle. I can only see relatively high context
> switching/system calls rate, that sometimes grows twice - up to
> 15K/30K. Is it too much?
